    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2T6Lp34YgtLAxRHPWVaj2wS)_\n\nBuilds on #332 (`M-x sp-litnotes-meta-status-report`).\n\n## What changes\n- With an active region (shift-select lines with `S-<down>`/`S-<up>`, works with CUA mode), `m` and `u` mark or unmark every note in it.\n- `s` changes the read-status of the marked notes; with no marks it now uses the region, else the note at point.\n- A region ending at the start of a line does not include that line. The region is deactivated afterwards.\n- Literate doc updated (bullets); new ERT test `sp-litnotes-meta-status-region-marks`.\n\n## Testing\n- `sp-litnotes-meta` ERT tests pass (13/13, Emacs 29.3). `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n- Not tried interactively in a GUI Emacs with CUA mode.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy). Branch is the session's designated name, not number-prefixed, since the PR number was unknown beforehand.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBEorDWGtrczAiFmRg)_",
